WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.096 --> 00:00:01.290
- 1.6 million.

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.670
That's the number of people killed

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:06.060
by fungal infections
worldwide in a single year.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.170
In 2021, at least 7,000 of
those deaths were in the U.S.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:13.590
That's more than 15
times as many as in 1969.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.617
We're not speeding towards

00:00:14.617 --> 00:00:16.443
"The Last of Us" fungal apocalypse,

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.250
but health experts are worried
about the growing number

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.530
of severe fungal infections,
the kind that infect

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.540
the blood and attack
the lungs and the brain.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.820
Let's go over three main reasons why fungi

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.170
are becoming more of a threat

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.270
and why it could get even worse.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.480
Climate change may be having
an impact on fungal evolution.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.900
This map from 2017 shows the
states that reported cases

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.510
of candida auris, an often deadly fungus.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.400
Fast forward a few years,

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.260
not only has candida auris spread

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.610
beyond a handful of states,

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.060
but as you can see, the case
count has also skyrocketed.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.430
The spread to more
places is also happening

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.110
with other severe fungal infections,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.360
like histoplasmosis and valley fever.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.880
- Their range has really exploded

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.010
over the last 50 years or so.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.290
- Fungi, whether it's
ones you eat like these,

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.430
or the ones that make you sick

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.660
when their breather spores in,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.960
they like temperatures that
are warm but not too hot.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.380
So as the planet warms, places
that were too cold before

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.030
are becoming more fungi-friendly.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.090
They may also be adapting to
be more tolerant of high heat,

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.770
and that includes the human body.

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.350
- Possibly because they've
adapted to warmer temperatures.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.840
It seems like they've become
better at infecting us.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.180
- Some recent evidence for
that comes from this study

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.770
that Dominique told me about.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.740
In a lab, scientists grew
hundreds of generations

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.440
of a fungus called
cryptococcus deneoformans.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.380
Some were grown at 98.6
degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.970
Others at 86 degrees.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.910
- It seemed that heat
and hotter temperatures

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.150
was really triggering them to mutate more.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.800
- The fungi were adapting.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.330
Scientists have been documented

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.940
this kind of heat-driven
evolution in the wild yet,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.380
but that may be because this area

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.390
of research is just so new.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.950
For most of human existence,

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.960
we've coexisted peacefully with fungi.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.330
- It seems like they
might help us digest food,

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.470
maybe even fight disease.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.700
Fungi are all around us.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.650
They help connect our forests.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.200
They break down our dead things.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.600
Like they're just so critical to life.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.430
- It's only recently that they've become

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.620
more worrisome pathogens.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:14.490
Ironically, one reason for
this shift is modern medicine.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.590
Better treatments for a range of diseases

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.960
has made it possible for
people to live longer,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.780
even when their immune systems
aren't working optimally.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.210
Infectious fungi are
particularly dangerous

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.280
for people with
compromised immune systems,

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.380
like patients who are going
through cancer treatment,

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.180
have advanced HIV infections,

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.430
or are taking high doses of steroids.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:36.060
By some estimates, almost
3% of the U.S. population

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.500
is immunocompromised.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.140
And this population is expected to grow.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.990
Adding to the problem is that
we don't have a lot of options

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:45.630
for treating severe fungal infections.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.700
It's hard to develop
treatments that kill fungi

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.300
without also being toxic to
humans, even at low doses.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.270
That's because fungal cells
are similar to human ones.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.700
- The fungi that are
currently causing disease

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.410
have developed resistance

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.050
to a lot of these known antifungals.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.180
- This new study showed
there were three times

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.870
as many resistant candida
auris infections in 2021

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.210
as in each of the previous two years.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.490
The pipeline for new drugs is also limited

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.050
because of a lack of investment,

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.220
but that's starting to change.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.560
- So I think there has been more interest

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.230
from pharmaceutical
companies, from researchers

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.190
to really look at this as
a potential area of R&amp;D,

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.960
but it's still kind of burgeoning.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.730
- And there are drugs and clinical trials

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.080
from several companies.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.180
It's important to
remember that even though

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.310
the threat from fungi is growing,

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.490
dying from a fungal infection
is still pretty rare.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:38.067
This study estimated that in 2019,

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:40.500
7.7 million people died globally

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.270
from infections caused by bacteria

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.640
like e.coli and staph aureus.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.560
That's almost five times as many

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.390
as have died because of a fungus.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.670
And on a lighter note,
if you're still scared

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:52.500
that a fungus that looks like this

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.990
can turn you and your
friends into zombies-

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.240
- There's no indication
that that's gonna happen.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:00.750
At least not any time in
the next few million years.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.420
Fungi have to really evolve
to be able to do that.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.433
- Whew, that's a relief.

